-- title:
--   Left Tensor Normalization Condition Sandwich Adjoint Bound
-- statement:
--   **The adjoint-side left-tensor sandwich family satisfies the normalization bound.**
--
--   Let $P=(P_a)_{a\in\alpha}$ be a submeasurement and let $Q=(Q_b)_{b\in\beta}$ be a projective submeasurement, with finite outcome sets $\alpha$ and $\beta$. Define
--
--   $$
--   C_a=\sum_{b\in\beta}(Q_bP_aQ_b)\otimes I
--   $$
--
--   on the first tensor register. Then the adjoint products obey
--
--   $$
--   \sum_{a\in\alpha}C_a^\dagger C_a\le I.
--   $$
--
--   This is the adjoint-side tensor-lifted normalization condition used as the $C$-normalization hypothesis in `closenessOfIPAdjoint`.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Commutativity.leftTensor_normalizationCondition_sandwich_adjoint_bound`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/LionSR/MIPStarRE/blob/f382c801026f53a9efc260fdee707cb35e0adb15/MIPStarRE/LDT/Commutativity/Transport/FullSlice/Machinery/Normalization.lean#L104-L143

